<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <DUT Name="ST_PendingEvent" Id="{abbfd234-3623-42a3-aa27-c85d027ac193}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[TYPE ST_PendingEvent :
(*
    ST_PendingEvent - one slot of FB_Listener's pending-event buffer.

    PURPOSE
        Hold one event that FB_Listener has accepted but not yet published.
        When an alarm, message, confirmation or clear fires, StoreEvent captures
        the event's severity, id, class, timestamp, source, type and JSON
        attributes in stEventInfo and starts an asynchronous request for the
        human-readable event text. The JSON document cannot be sent until that
        text has arrived, so the event waits in this slot instead of blocking
        the calling PLC task.

    USAGE
        Never instantiated on its own. FB_Listener declares
        stPendingEvents : ARRAY [0..nMaxEvents - 1] OF ST_PendingEvent
        (nMaxEvents is the fixed number of events handled per cycle) and walks it
        as a ring buffer.

        Writer - FB_Listener.StoreEvent: scans forward from nEventIdx until it
        finds a slot whose bInUse is FALSE, claims that slot
        (bInUse := TRUE, nPendingEvents + 1), fills stEventInfo and calls
        fbRequestEventText.Request(...).

        Reader - FB_Listener.PublishEvents: for every slot with bInUse = TRUE it
        waits until fbRequestEventText is no longer busy, copies the text into
        stEventInfo.msg through GetString, builds the JSON document and sends it,
        then frees the slot (bInUse := FALSE, nPendingEvents - 1) and leaves
        nEventIdx pointing at it so the next StoreEvent reuses it first.

        A slot therefore lives over several PLC cycles: claimed in the cycle the
        event arrives, published once the logger has produced the text. When all
        slots are still claimed, StoreEvent reports "Logging message buffer full"
        and drops the event.

    OBJECTIVES
        - Keep event logging asynchronous, so a slow Tc3_EventLogger text
          request never stalls the calling PLC task.
        - Bind an event's metadata and its text request together in one slot, so
          the text that finally arrives is matched to the event it belongs to.
        - Give FB_Listener a fixed, statically sized buffer with an explicit
          occupancy flag instead of dynamic allocation.
        - Make the pending buffer inspectable online: the bInUse flags of
          stPendingEvents show how many events are in flight.

    HISTORY
        2019-11-12 / K Lauer
            Type added with the rewrite of the logging system onto
            Tc3_EventLogger (asynchronous event-text retrieval).
        2020-01-09 / K Lauer
            Event info member retyped to the pinned global ST_LoggingEventInfo.
        2021-11-02 / K Lauer
            Style pass: pre-commit run --all-files (whitespace); no logic change.
        2023-05-22 / Jakob Sagatowski
            Removed the "Write product version in files" flag from the projects.
        2026-11-28 / Scirix Agent
            Added this header and the member comments below; type layout and
            behaviour unchanged (audit finding #1080, convention
            conv_321640e095c0).
*)
STRUCT

    // Event metadata copied from the FB_TcEvent by FB_Listener.StoreEvent: id
    // (UDINT event id), event_class (GUID as string), severity, ts (Unix
    // timestamp, seconds), source, event_type and json (the event's JSON
    // attributes as an escaped string). PublishEvents adds plc (host name) and
    // msg (the retrieved text). Values carry the logger's own units, so no
    // scaling is applied here.
    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv:
    '}
    stEventInfo			:	ST_LoggingEventInfo;

    // Slot occupancy flag, not a state: FALSE by default, set TRUE the moment
    // FB_Listener.StoreEvent claims this slot, and reset to FALSE by
    // PublishEvents once the slot's JSON has been sent. The only member that
    // marks the slot as taken; stEventInfo and fbRequestEventText are only
    // meaningful while it is TRUE.
    bInUse				:	BOOL;

    // Asynchronous retrieval of this event's human-readable text from the
    // TwinCAT event logger (FB_RequestEventText, Tc3_EventLogger). StoreEvent
    // starts it with the event class, event id, language id 1033 and the event's
    // arguments; PublishEvents polls bBusy and, once it drops, copies the text
    // into stEventInfo.msg with GetString(). If bError is set the published msg
    // reads "(Unable to retrieve message)". The text buffer lives in this
    // instance, which is why it has to move together with the slot.
    fbRequestEventText	:	FB_RequestEventText;

END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>